{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Strike_(Defect)","to":"Strike (Defect)"},{"from":"Just_Lucky","to":"Just Lucky"},{"from":"Battle_Hymn","to":"Battle Hymn"},{"from":"Live_Forever","to":"Live Forever"},{"from":"Sucker_Punch","to":"Sucker Punch"}],"pages":{"2419":{"pageid":2419,"ns":0,"title":"Battle Hymn","revisions":[{"revid":56894,"parentid":55639,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Battle Hymn\n|Image       = Purple-BattleHymn.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. <br>)At the start of each turn, add a {{C|Smite}} into your hand.\n|GivesToPlayer = Innate\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Battle Hymn}} {{Small Card Infobox|Smite}}\n{{C|Battle Hymn}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives one {{BD|Battle Hymn}}, which adds one {{C|Smite}} to your hand at the start of every turn. When upgraded, it becomes {{KW|Innate}}, If this card is upgraded, it becomes {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always be in the first hand of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Battle Hymn}} takes effect before your cards are drawn. This means that having a high amount of {{BD|Battle Hymn}} can cause you to draw less cards at the start of your turn due to the hand size limit.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have played {{C|Master Reality}} before playing this card, it will add upgraded {{C|Smite|Smites}} to your hand instead.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{C|Smite}} generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* The constant addition of {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards to your hand will make it harder to play {{C|Signature Move}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2293":{"pageid":2293,"ns":0,"title":"Just Lucky","revisions":[{"revid":50648,"parentid":36371,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Just Lucky\n|Image       = Purple-JustLucky.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Scry}} (1;2). <br>Gain (2;3) {{KW|Block}}. <br>Deal (3;4) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Just Lucky}} is a 0 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It allows you to {{KW|Scry}} 1 (2 if upgraded). It gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and deals 3 (4 if upgraded) damage.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have {{R|Golden Eye}}, you will be able to {{KW|Scry}} 2 more cards.\n* Playing {{C|Just Lucky}} will activate {{C|Nirvana}}.\n* As it allows you to {{KW|Scry}}, any {{C|Weave}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand. \n** If a {{C|Weave}} is among the cards {{KW|Scry|Scryed}} by {{C|Just Lucky}} and is discarded this way, it will immediately be brought back into your hand.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows the gremlin from the event {{E|Wheel of Change}} getting what he deserves.\n** He knows what he did.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2379":{"pageid":2379,"ns":0,"title":"Live Forever","revisions":[{"revid":53298,"parentid":50771,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"#REDIRECT [[Wish#Live Forever]]"}}}]},"2114":{"pageid":2114,"ns":0,"title":"Multi-Cast","revisions":[{"revid":55864,"parentid":50625,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Multi-Cast\n|Image       = Blue-Multi-Cast.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = {{KW|Evoke}} your next Orb (X;X+1) times.\n}}\n{{C|Multi-Cast}} is an X {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* If {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orb}} {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} by {{C|Tempest}} causes you to gain {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''', the value of X will not change and that newly generated {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' will not be consumed.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Multi-Cast can repeatedly {{KW|Evoke}} the same large {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb}} for massive damage.\n* When {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} a {{KW|Lightning}} or {{KW|Frost}} Orb, {{BD|Focus}} can substantially improve Multi-Casts output: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Multi-Cast}} apply 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If played through an effect such as {{P|Distilled Chaos}} or {{C|Mayhem}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}} or {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Multi-Cast}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Burst}}, the value of X will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Multi-Cast}} can be {{C|Recycle|Recycled}} to double the current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|Scrape}} or {{C|All for One}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 53: Blizzard'''\n** Fixed issue where evoked Dark Orbs wouldn't switch targets if the first target died when multi-casting.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Corruption and other cost reducing cards no longer make X cost cards like Transmutation and Malaise display cost 0.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1920":{"pageid":1920,"ns":0,"title":"Normality","revisions":[{"revid":56746,"parentid":55872,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Normality\n| Image       = Curse-Normality.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>While in hand, you cannot play more than 3 cards this turn.\n| GivesToPlayer = Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Normality}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. While it is in your hand, you can only play up to 3 cards in a turn.\n\n== Obtaining Normality ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Normality can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Normality can be obtained from the {{E|Mind Bloom}} Event when choosing {{Frame|I am Rich}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Normality only prevents further card plays while actively in the hand. If, for instance you draw and then discard it in a single card play, such as with {{C|Acrobatics}} or {{C|Scrape}}, your turn can continue as normal.\n* As drawing for the turn happens before {{C|Mayhem}}, Normality can prevent Mayhem from playing more than 3 cards.\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Normality is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP.\n** However, doing so counts as playing a card, so you can only do this if you've played less than 3 cards so far this turn.\n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\nNormality's unique downside is often very problematic. However, some effects can mitigate the downside:\n* It can be discarded away with {{C|Acrobatics}}, {{C|Survivor}}, {{C|Prepared}}, {{C|Dagger Throw}}, {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, {{C|All-Out Attack}}, {{C|Concentrate}}, {{C|Storm of Steel}}, {{C|Tools of the Trade}}, {{C|Unload}}, {{R|Gambling Chip}}, and {{P|Gambler's Brew}}.\n* In addition to Blue Candle, it can be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} with {{C|Havoc}}, {{C|True Grit}}, {{C|Burning Pact}}, {{C|Second Wind}}, {{C|Sever Soul}}, {{C|Fiend Fire}}, {{C|Purity}}, and {{P|Elixir}}.\n* {{R|Pocketwatch}} can draw you additional cards after a turn where you end up stuck with Normality in your hand.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Drawing into Normality after playing more than 3 cards in a turn has no additional effect; it simply shuts off further card plays as usual.\n* Multiple copies of Normality do not stack; you can still only play 3 cards in a turn.\n* Double playing a card by any means ({{P|Duplication Potion}}, {{C|Echo Form}}, etc.) counts as '''two plays''' for all purposes. If the second play would be your fourth card for the turn, the card will not be played.\n* Cards played by {{P|Distilled Chaos}} and similar effects are still counted for Normality. If such an effect would go past 3 card plays for the turn, the remainder will simply be discarded.\n* The effect of Normality is '''not a [[Debuff]]''', and cannot be bypassed with {{BD|Artifact}} or {{R|Orange Pellets}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Normality, it cannot be played.\n* {{C|Regret}} and Normality synergize in a harmful fashion; only being able to play 3 cards means there are more cards left in your hand when Regret goes off.\n* Cards that generate lots of {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}, such as {{C|Blade Dance}}, {{C|Cloak and Dagger}}, and {{C|Storm of Steel}} tend to be dangerous to play with Normality in hand, as you take your entire turn for one card and/or end up shuffling Shivs into your deck.\n* Cards that generate Energy when played, and especially those that draw cards as well, are likely to be wasted due to Normality: {{C|Offering}}, {{C|Doppelganger}}, {{C|Adrenaline}}, and {{C|Fission}}.\n\n<!---\n== Trivia ==\nNormality suxxxxxxxx\n--->\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1437":{"pageid":1437,"ns":0,"title":"Strike (Defect)","revisions":[{"revid":50548,"parentid":43237,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation|1|1}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Strike (Defect)\n|DisplayName = Strike\n|Image       = Blue-Strike.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Basic\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (6;9) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Strike (Defect)|Strike}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 (9 if upgraded) damage.\n\nThis page is for Defect's version of Strike. Go here for {{C|Strike (Ironclad)}}, {{C|Strike (Silent)}}, {{C|Strike (Watcher)}}.\n\n== Obtaining Strike ==\nThe [[Defect]] starts with 4 copies of {{C|Strike (Defect)|Strike}} in their deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Strike (Defect)|Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Defect's Strikes now use the impact VFX and SFX instead of Slicing effects.\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Fixed issue where Strike (blue), Thunder Strike, and Meteor Strike weren't used by Perfected Strike.\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2024":{"pageid":2024,"ns":0,"title":"Sucker Punch","revisions":[{"revid":55964,"parentid":50492,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Sucker Punch\n|Image       = Green-SuckerPunch.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;9) damage.<br>Apply (1;2) {{BD|Weak}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}}\n{{C|Sucker Punch}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (9 if upgraded) damage and applies 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Krane}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1454":{"pageid":1454,"ns":0,"title":"Survivor","revisions":[{"revid":56335,"parentid":55504,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Survivor\n| Image       = Green-Survivor.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (8;11) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Discard 1 card.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block, Discard\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Survivor}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 8 (11 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and makes you select 1 card in hand to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]]. If there are no other cards in hand when this card is played, no card will be [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n\n== Obtaining Survivor ==\nThe [[Silent]] starts the game with one copy of {{C|Survivor}} in her deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards, but can be obtained in the {{E|Match and Keep}} Event. \n\n== Interactions == \n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Survivor}}'s [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics: \n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' this turn.\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy.\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Survivor}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 45: Impatience'''\n** Fixed exploit that allowed player to circumvent hand card confirmations (like Survivor).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Discard/Draw panels can be viewed during screens such as Survivor, Headbutt, and Gambling Chip now.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2043":{"pageid":2043,"ns":0,"title":"Terror","revisions":[{"revid":55973,"parentid":50524,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Terror\n|Image       = Green-Terror.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Apply 99 {{BD|Vulnerable}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Terror}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|GE}}-cost. {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It apples 99 {{BD|Vulnerable}} to the chosen enemy and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} when played.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* The entire effect of this card will be negated by 1 {{BD|Artifact}} on the target.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The beta design of Terror is based on the painting \"The Scream\" by Edvard Munch.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2418":{"pageid":2418,"ns":0,"title":"Vault","revisions":[{"revid":56055,"parentid":55993,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Vault\n|Image       = Purple-Vault.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|CostPlus    = 2\n|Description = Take an extra turn after this one. <br>End your turn. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Vault}} is a 3 (2 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It ends your turn, and skips every part of the enemy's turn, as well as the end of the round, bringing it immediately to the start of your turn again. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Anything that triggers, decreases or wears off at any part of your turn still functions as normal, for example:\n** Your {{KW|Block}} is removed as normal.\n** Any form of {{KW|Retain}}, such as through {{BD|Well-Laid Plans}} or {{BD|Equilibrium}} triggers, as well as {{BD|Establishment}} reducing the cost of these {{KW|Retain|Retained}} cards.\n** Effects such as {{BD|Double Tap}}, {{BD|Rebound}} and {{BD|Entangled}} wear off.\n** You will lose {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Dexterity}} through effects such as {{BD|Strength Down}} or {{BD|Wraith Form}}.\n** You will exit the Divinity {{KW|Stance}}. \n** Damaging effects, such as {{BD|Omega}} or {{BD|The Bomb}} deal damage as normal.\n\n* Anything that triggers, decreases, wears off or resets at any point of the enemy's turn is skipped.\n** Anything mentioned in the previous block is skipped if it belongs to an enemy instead of the player.\n** Enemies keep their {{KW|Block}}\n** [[Byrd|Byrds]] do not reset their {{BD|Flying}} and the [[Corrupt Heart]] does not reset its {{BD|Invincible}}\n\n* Anything that triggers, decreases, wears off or resets at the end of the round is skipped. \n** {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Vulnerable}}, {{BD|Weak}} and {{BD|Lock-On}} do not decrease.\n** {{BD|Blur}}, {{BD|Double Damage}}, {{BD|Equilibrium}}, {{BD|Intangible}}, and {{BD|No Block}} do not decrease, although their effects still apply as normal.\n** {{BD|Draw Reduction}}, {{P|Duplication Potion}}, and {{BD|Wave of the Hand}} do not wear off, although their effects still apply as normal.\n** A [[Cultist]]'s {{BD|Ritual}} and a [[Orb Walker]]'s {{BD|Strength Up}} do not trigger. \n** {{BD|Malleable}} and {{BD|Slow}} do not reset.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} that trigger every turn, for example {{C|Deva Form}}'s {{BD|Deva}} will scale. \n* Scales any {{C|Perseverance}}, {{C|Sands of Time}}, and {{C|Windmill Strike}} that is {{KW|Retain|Retained}}.\n* {{C|Vault}} can be used to negate the forced end of turn of {{BD|Time Warp}} if played as the 12th card, as well as the card limit of {{R|Velvet Choker}} or {{C|Normality}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Playing this card twice through an effect like {{C|Omniscience}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}} will result in that effect being wasted, as the first copy played already ends your turn, preventing the second play.\n* {{BD|Draw Reduction}} applies but does not wear off, meaning playing {{C|Vault}} while having this debuff makes it affect you twice. \n* {{C|Blasphemy}}'s {{BD|Blasphemer}} will trigger immediately.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}